<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Info.plist — Shell Citadel

    THIS FILE EXISTS FOR EXACTLY ONE KEY, and it is worth saying why so nobody deletes it
    while tidying up.

    Every other Info.plist entry in this project is set as an INFOPLIST_KEY_* build
    setting in project.pbxproj, which is the modern shape and keeps the settings in one
    place. That mechanism can only express FLAT keys — `INFOPLIST_KEY_Foo` becomes `Foo`.

    `NSLocationTemporaryUsageDescriptionDictionary` is a DICTIONARY. It maps a purpose key
    to the sentence iOS shows when an app asks to borrow full location accuracy for one
    operation, and there is no build-setting spelling for a nested value. So this file is
    the base plist, GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE stays YES, and the flat keys are merged in on
    top of it at build time.

    ⚠️ The purpose key below MUST match `LocationStamp.pinDropPurposeKey`. A mismatch does
    not crash and does not warn — the request just returns denied, silently, which is the
    exact failure shape this project has been bitten by before.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSLocationTemporaryUsageDescriptionDictionary</key>
	<dict>
		<key>PinDrop</key>
		<string>Dropping a pin needs your exact location for this one map picture. Your normal messages only carry your general area, and your location is never sent anywhere except your own Mac.</string>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
